[00:29.75]The long day loosens at the water's edge
[00:37.03]The birch doth cast a longer shadow now
[00:44.48]We gather on the stones where we were born
[00:50.96]Beneath the greying northern evening sky

[00:59.33]Sumar snýr — the summer turneth slow
[01:05.59]The light that would not sleep begins to close its eye
[01:13.28]One last evening the whole coast doth hold its breath
[01:20.30]Before the fires, before the long goodbye

[01:28.61]Vér kveikjum eldana — we shall light the fires
[01:36.05]Ljós á vatni — light upon the sea!

[01:43.03]Come down! Come down to the water and the stones!
[01:50.09]Come down where the whole of the coast doth gather in!
[01:56.50]For the dark is patient — but so are we!
[02:03.93]One more night! One more night of light — begin!
[02:11.81]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir!
[02:15.45]The summer thou didst give!
[02:18.89]One last evening we shall hold it!
[02:21.97]One last evening we shall live!

[02:33.74]The nets are drawn, the boats are turned to shore
[02:39.70]The children carry driftwood down the sand
[02:46.72]The old ones bring the lanterns from the sheds
[02:53.72]And no word passeth — all doth understand

[building again, slower this time, weight gathering]
[03:01.99]Vér kveikjum eldana — we shall light the fires
[03:09.25]Ljós á vatni — light upon the sea!

[03:16.48]Come down! Come down to the water and the stones!
[03:23.19]Come down where the whole of the coast doth gather in!
[03:29.59]For the dark is patient — but so are we!
[03:36.88]One more night! One more night of light — begin!
[03:44.92]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir!
[03:48.40]The summer thou didst give!
[03:51.68]One last evening we shall hold it!
[03:55.03]One last evening we shall live!

[04:28.22]Kveldrøkkr...
[04:31.81]The gathering dusk...
[04:35.60]Ljós á vatni...
